 "title": "Error provenance is carried by string sniffing",
 "description": "Error provenance is carried by string sniffing. Own-rule errors are tagged with the literal prefix `jev::v1: ` (OWN_MESSAGE) inside a serde error message, and `describe` recovers them with `strip_prefix`. `TryFrom<RawJevQuestion>` and `TryFrom<RawQuestion>` use `type Error = String`, which flattens the structured JevError (via `detail()`) back into text. Any serde message that happens to start with the prefix is treated as safe to show, and the error structure is lost across layers.",
